WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:09.810
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:20.340
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.530
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:07.010
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:14.280
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.020
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:28.450
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.190
Get a move on!

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.700
You say it’s a Simoun from Arcus Niger?

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.330
Military Councilor!

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.700
What’s the meaning of this!

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.290
Arcus Niger…

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.490
…was shot down.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.330
What?

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:52.040
Seven o’clock! Five ancient
Simouns approaching fast!

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.170
What in the world?

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.730
<b>Sortie</b>

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.100
Four o’clock! Multiple aircraft sighted!

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.230
Hurry, confirm that!

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.960
They appear to be
Shoukoku cruise missiles!

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.400
Vura, take one of the similes.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.360
Right.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.200
Which way should we head?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.830
She’s right. They say the
enemy Simouns are here too!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.290
We’re going to destroy the
missiles headed toward the city!

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.040
What about the Highland Simouns?

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.290
Arcus Prima and the Messis…

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.040
…will have to meet the
attack without our protection.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.130
Para-sama…

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.420
Kaim…

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.110
We have to give it our best shot.
That’s all we can do now!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.050
Right!

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.110
Falcon Ri Majon!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.610
Falcon Ri Majon!

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.360
Falcon Ri Majon!

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.080
Nine o’clock! More aircraft approaching!

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.580
Tell me what they are and how many!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.580
Shoukoku cruise missiles!
Twenty of them!

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.460
Roatreamon! Three o’clock,
more missiles headed our way!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.600
Right.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.830
What’s wrong?

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.260
Oh, it’s nothing…

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.450
Whether it’s a Ri Majon to
honor the souls of the dead…

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.520
…or a Ri Majon to repulse the enemy…

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.940
…a Ri Majon is still a Ri Majon.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.480
That’s what I used to believe.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.190
Morinas…

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.560
— Para-sama!
— Come on!

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.730
Para-sama, the shrapnel
is falling over the town!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.070
There’s just too many of them!

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.530
Para-sama, look!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.300
But now I know that’s not true at all.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.380
Yes, they’re both Ri Majons, but they’re
for a completely different purpose!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.510
Hold on tight!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.790
Morinas!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.440
Morinas!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.890
Are you two all right?

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.360
Morinas is hurt…

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.620
Don’t worry. It’s nothing. What about
you, Roatreamon? Are you all right?

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.330
Yes, I’m fine.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.870
Paraietta, what about the enemy Simouns?

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.670
The thing is… I can’t be sure, but…

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.340
They seem to have flown off.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.870
What’s that?

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.670
They’re turning around and flying away.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.090
Are you absolutely sure?

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.060
The Plumbum enemy Simouns
are about to leave our sights!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.390
Why?

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.560
Why didn’t the enemy Simouns attack us?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.900
I know. But if they had attacked us,
they might have gotten us.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.450
Guragief?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.490
Yes?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.500
Your quarters, please.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.540
What?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.380
Well?

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.730
What’s going on?

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.020
Military Councilor?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.270
Anubituf, what’s going on?

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:24.360
The simile transporting Sibylla
Mamina’s body never returned.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:26.460
No…

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.610
I’m certain it was
intercepted by the enemy.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.240
Needless to say, this happened
within the Kyuukoku borders.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.330
Meaning we’ve already lost
control of our own airspace.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.870
Then…

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.670
…what about Sibylla Mamina’s body?

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:46.590
Guragief, that hardly matters anymore!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.450
— Can’t you see we’re in a state of…
— So it’s no concern of ours…

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.950
…what happens to Sibylla Mamina’s
body. Is that what you’re saying, sir?

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.290
Guragief…

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:57.600
You are not to inform the
sibyllae of this matter.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.980
Anubituf!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.600
I don’t believe this! Even you…

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.230
The fact that the enemy Simouns
showed up in battle today…

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:10.070
…was a taunt to let us know
they can attack us at any time.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.370
And that’s exactly
what they’re capable of.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:30.690
No way…

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:34.550
I can’t believe such a thing
could’ve happened while we were gone.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.880
There must be something
we can do to help.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.680
Right!

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.860
Come in!

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.370
How are you holding up, Sibylla Morinas?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.940
Waporif!

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.620
Waporif, are you good
at wrapping bandages?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.330
I had no idea Roatreamon
was so bad at this.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.260
Please, allow me, Sibylla Roatreamon.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.510
You see, the doctor was busy, so…

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.090
He’s gone to the great temple,
tending to the injured civilians.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.760
I see.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.890
Well, I’m leaving her
in your hands then.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:21.930
Fine.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.810
Morinas…

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.320
We still have a lot of
things to do, don’t we?

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.070
Sure.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:37.030
Still, I like the Ri Majons
that we offer to Tempus Spatium.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.030
Yeah, so do I.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.580
And you know what? I bet
everyone else feels the same way!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.120
Right!

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.800
How bad is the damage to the Simoun?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.760
Looks like we’ll only
have to replace the canopy.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.930
We just finished repairing Sibylla
Aurea’s Simoun, and now this…

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.650
I’m sorry.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.890
Was there no other way?

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.780
No, there really wasn’t.

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:16.110
I want you to take
better care of yourself.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.660
All right, I will.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.030
Promise me.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.790
I promise.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.490
Let me ask you one more time.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:51.570
There is no longer any way to engage
the Shoukoku-highlands alliance…

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.830
Is that what you’re saying?

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:55.640
You were the one…

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.700
…who took away three of the Simoun
sibyllae at such a critical time.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.580
Let’s be clear about
who’s responsible for this!

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:05.290
I believe the situation is well
past the point of assigning blame.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.540
We really should return to
the purpose of this meeting.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.220
One hour ago, the
Shoukoku-highlands alliance…

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:18.580
…offered Simulacrum
Kyuukoku a cease-fire.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.930
Now that they have a
clear advantage over us…

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.310
…they’re actually suing for peace?

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.530
Don’t tell me you’ve
already forgotten how…

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.600
…the highlands negotiated
peace the last time.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:32.520
But it is our people’s desire to bring
an end to this war as soon as possible!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.780
Can’t you see that their
offer is nothing but a sham?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:36.780
Not again…
\h

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.800
This wouldn’t have happened…

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.180
…if you’d tried to negotiate peacefully.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.240
I’ve had enough of your petty grudges!
\h

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.280
How dare you!

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.120
I…

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.290
I’m not fit for this…

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.540
That’s not true, Aer.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.370
No matter what you may think
yourself, you are a Simoun sibylla.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.300
All I know is war.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.840
I don’t know anything about praying.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:04.950
Amuria…

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:06.810
She was a warrior too.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:13.460
Even so, her prayers brought
solace to many people.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:17.400
Everyone flocked to
Amuria to be blessed.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:23.490
The priestesses are going
to protect us, right?

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.630
The priestesses are going to
strike down all the bad guys!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.960
That’s right. Just be
patient a little while longer.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.180
Okay!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.560
I’m so sorry. I didn’t
think you’d be here.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.470
That’s all right.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:12:00.560
Neviril and Aer are
blessing the people outside.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.070
Yes, I know.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.570
Who ever thought we’d
see Aer doing that?

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.410
Really!

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.620
You’re the one we’d expect to
take the initiative… Oh…

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.820
Yes, that’s true.

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:24.760
Mamina…

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.970
I think she should be by your side, Yun.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:30.210
Why is that?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.350
I can’t really explain why…

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.860
…but I want you to
hold on to this for me.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.450
So…

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.730
Yun, will you look after
Mamina for me from now on?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.300
Fine.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.040
I never thought you’d
hide anything from me.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.810
Neither did I.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.860
What is it that you want from me?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.530
I just don’t know anymore!

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.780
What do I want from you?

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:40.280
Emergency! Guys, it’s an emergency!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.460
Neviril! Aer!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.090
Neviril!

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.800
Neviril! We just heard that they’re
asking for another peace treaty.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:54.140
Yes, Floe just told us.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.040
But is that information true?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.940
Yes, Sibylla Neviril.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:00.860
Guragief…

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.970
Did the information come from you then?

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:05.240
Only a handful of
people are aware of this.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.950
I took it upon myself to inform you all.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.370
I see.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.730
So is the war really
going to end this time?

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.150
I don’t know about that.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.930
Remember, Anglas was
supposed to be visiting…

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:21.630
…Kyuukoku as an interpreter
for the peace conference.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.090
I know, but maybe this time around…

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.420
Yes.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:29.630
It’s possible that this time we’ll be
able to release you sibyllae from battle.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.140
Whatever happens, there’s
nothing we can do about it.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.020
That’s right.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.860
We can only do what we
have the power to do.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.570
Guragief, I’d like to
discuss something with you…

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.450
Sibylla Aurea!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.220
Paraietta said the same thing just now!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.540
Did she?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:01.780
First off, to protect
ourselves from being invaded…

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.340
…from the mountains,
let us go out on patrol.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.270
I understand it’s a
state of emergency, but…

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.520
Just look at the size
of the Arcus Prima.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.820
Yes.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.860
I find it hard to believe that Arcus
Niger, a ship of the same dimensions…

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.660
…was actually shot down.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.020
Yes, indeed.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:31.280
Just as hard to believe as
seeing you at odds with Guragief!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.280
So you noticed?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.640
I can’t imagine the
depth of your feelings…

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:38.660
…for each other that
neither of you can concede.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.790
Guragief is…

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.330
…too single-minded.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.750
That’s for sure!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.700
It’s a shame that he
decided to become a man!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.990
Anubituf…

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:55.550
Try to make peace with
Guragief as soon as you can.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.870
You might not have a lot
of time left with him.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:15:59.880
Right.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.270
I have to get back to the bridge.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:05.900
Para-sama!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.110
Hurry, Kaim.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.530
But why are they attacking us again?

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.740
They’re going to keep at it
until they bend us to their will!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.240
Let’s go.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:23.120
Para-sama!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.090
Cast off the moorings!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.880
Drop anchor!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.010
Ascend at top speed! Hurry!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.470
Ascending at top speed.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.850
What’s going on?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.650
Seven o’clock! Five ancient
Simouns approaching!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:52.990
Eleven o’clock, Shoukoku
midrange aircraft approaching!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.610
Prepare the Simouns for takeoff!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.740
Yes, sir!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.460
Where are the priestesses
from Chor Tempest?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:05.900
They’re not here yet, sir.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:06.920
What?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.340
What are you waiting for, Anubituf?

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:12.380
Order Chor Tempest to go into battle!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.920
— Captain?
— Pay no attention to him.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.180
Anubituf!

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.520
Communications officer…

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.730
Send word for the sibyllae to
stand by on the flight deck.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.730
I’m going to convey my orders in person.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.650
Yes, sir!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:33.150
Guragief, I’m leaving
you in charge for now.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:36.000
The Arcus Prima will launch
the second wave of our attack.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.660
You’ll be directing
the Arcus Prima then.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.030
Understood!

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.750
I’ll be in command until
the captain returns.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:44.700
Yes, sir!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.670
What are you doing?
Get up there already!

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:51.050
Our orders are to stand
by on the flight deck.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.550
What the!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:57.040
Damn that Anubituf! What’s he thinking?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.600
— Standing by at a time like this!
— That old guy is so obnoxious!

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.760
Sorry to keep you waiting, sibyllae.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.520
Hold on, you…

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.520
Surprised?

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:16.030
It may be hard to believe, but I too
was once a sibylla just like all of you.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.940
You’re going to fly a Simile, then?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:23.540
Yes. We’re going to have to meet the
enemy attack with only five Simouns.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:28.330
I’m going up in a Simile and will
give you direct orders in the sky.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.750
Please follow those orders.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.690
Yes, sir! Understood!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.260
Sibylla Morinas…

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.930
How is your wound?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:41.800
I was given impeccable
treatment, sir. Everything is fine!

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.970
Get that Simile ready to go. Now!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:45.770
Yes, sir!

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.370
Sibyllae…

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:10.490
The time has come for
us to take you out…

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:12.710
…of this war that you’ve
been fighting for us.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:17.130
But only because we have failed…

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.380
We thank you, Captain Anubituf.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.430
No matter what happens, we
shall never forget your words.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:27.640
Yeah, no need to worry!
We’ve already made up our minds!

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:29.520
We’re just going to
give it our best shot…

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.350
What we have the power to do!

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.360
We’re hopelessly outnumbered.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.460
We’re going to draw them
in as close as we can…

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.360
…then make a sudden
dive and strike them hard!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:49.250
This first attack will
decide the course of battle!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.170
Let’s go!

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:19.070
Follow me!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.170
All batteries, fire at will!

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.100
They’re escaping!

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:04.570
That’ll show you, losers!

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:06.910
Right?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.030
Hey…

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:09.950
How do you like that, jerks?

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.550
Both of you, watch your language!

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.790
You heard us?

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:21.310
No, but we were just saying that
you two were probably talking vulgar!

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.710
Thanks a lot!

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.300
Good work, everyone.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.060
Hey, what’s going on?

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:30.510
Yes, tell us!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:33.600
I’ll bet it’s just Floe making
another one of her absurd comments.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:36.390
Yeah, that’s probably
it, huh, Para-sama?

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:37.560
That’s insulting!

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:39.690
I never said anything like that!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.010
Is Chor Tempest always like this?

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.570
Pretty much.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.870
The Captain’s Simile, approaching!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.830
Everybody, hats off!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:20.730
Despite Chor Tempest’s efforts…

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.980
…the center determined that
the war was now a lost cause.

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:28.060
And several days later…

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:33.540
…accepted the peace treaty offered
by the Plumbum highlands and Shoukoku.

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:47.930
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:52.170
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:59.240
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:06.840
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.730
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:24.900
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:28.880
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:32.920
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:38.790
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:44.330
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:47.760
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:53.430
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:59.660
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.450 --> 00:24:10.510
As alliance soldiers take
control of the Arcus Prima…

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:13.130
…Chor Tempest is disbanded.

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:15.550
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>Eternal Maidens</b>

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:17.950
Eternal Maidens.
